What it is based on
-------------------

sketch-orca is a modified version of OrcaSlicer, by the OrcaSlicer contributors:

    https://github.com/OrcaSlicer/OrcaSlicer
    tag v2.4.2, commit 8500fcdccaa10b5099ac20d252af3a7c560046f1 (orca.lock.json)
    licensed under the GNU Affero General Public License, version 3

OrcaSlicer is based on Bambu Studio and carries work from SuperSlicer, each licensed under the
GNU Affero General Public License, version 3:

  - Bambu Studio, by Bambu Lab (https://github.com/bambulab/BambuStudio), is based on PrusaSlicer.
  - PrusaSlicer, owned by Prusa Research (https://github.com/prusa3d/PrusaSlicer), is originally
    based on Slic3r.
  - Slic3r was created by Alessandro Ranellucci with the help of many other contributors and the
    RepRap community (https://github.com/Slic3r/Slic3r).
  - SuperSlicer, by supermerill and contributors (https://github.com/supermerill/SuperSlicer),
    extends PrusaSlicer; OrcaSlicer carries some of its features.

Code of others in the OrcaSlicer tree, as OrcaSlicer credits it:

  - ArcWelderLib, by Brad Hochgesang, under the GNU Affero General Public License, version 3 or
    (at your option) any later version: the arc fitting of src/libslic3r/Geometry/ArcWelder.cpp.
  - The pressure advance calibration pattern, adapted by OrcaSlicer from Andrew Ellis' generator,
    which is itself adapted from a generator by Sineos for Marlin; both under the GNU General
    Public License, version 3.
  - The libraries OrcaSlicer pins as source packages (deps/) or keeps in its tree (deps_src/),
    each under its own licence. A staged engine carries their licence texts in LICENSES/deps and
    LICENSES/deps_src.

Code of others that this repository builds into the engine itself, or supplies the licence text
or the source of:

  - NanoSVG, by Mikko Mononen, under the zlib licence: cli/gui_symbols.cpp compiles its
    implementation from OrcaSlicer's copy (deps_src/nanosvg), whose notice is staged as
    LICENSES/deps_src/nanosvg/nanosvg.h.notice.txt.
  - libnoise, by Jason Bevins, under the GNU Lesser General Public License, version 2.1 or later:
    the package OrcaSlicer pins lacks the licence text, so licenses/LGPL-2.1.txt supplies it.
  - GMP 5.0.1 (the GNU Multiple Precision Arithmetic Library), by the Free Software Foundation,
    under the GNU Lesser General Public License, version 3 or later: OrcaSlicer ships it prebuilt
    for Windows, and the source bundle carries its source (BUILDING.md, "Prebuilt libraries").
  - OpenSSL 3.5.9, by the OpenSSL Project Authors, under the Apache License, version 2.0: libslic3r
    computes MD5 sums with its libcrypto, which the engine links statically. patches/0006 pins
