    LICENSES/deps/OpenSSL/LICENSE.txt, and the source bundle carries its source package.

On Windows the engine and the libraries it loads that are built from source (OpenCASCADE, FreeType)
are linked with Microsoft's static C and C++ runtime libraries, which come with the Visual C++
compiler (/MT; patches/0005). No Visual C++ runtime DLL is shipped with the engine.


What was changed, and when
--------------------------

All changes are dated, here and in the files. The staged engine's LICENSES/README.txt gives the
newest date of the patch headers.

  - patches/0001 to 0004 change OrcaSlicer's build files and one libslic3r source so that the
    slicing library builds without the GUI. Each patch's header, the lines before its diff, has a
    title line and then a dated "Modified for Sketch, <date>." line, and the lines it adds to
    OrcaSlicer's files carry a dated comment. Modified 2026-10-30.
  - patches/0005 and 0006 change OrcaSlicer's dependency build, in the same form: 0005 builds the
    dependencies with MSVC's static runtime library, and 0006 builds OpenSSL 3.5.9 instead of
    OpenSSL 1.1.1w. Modified 2026-11-01.
  - cli/ is the command-line front end, added 2026-10-30; its file headers and its usage text
    were changed on 2026-10-31, and cli/CMakeLists.txt on 2026-11-01 (MSVC's static runtime
    instead of copying its DLLs). Some of its files carry OrcaSlicer code, adapted, whose portions
    are copyright the OrcaSlicer contributors; each says which code from which OrcaSlicer file,
    under "Carries OrcaSlicer code":
      cli/run.cpp           (src/OrcaSlicer.cpp, src/slic3r/GUI/PartPlate.cpp, src/slic3r/GUI/Plater.cpp)
      cli/presets.cpp       (src/OrcaSlicer.cpp, src/slic3r/GUI/Plater.cpp, src/slic3r/GUI/BitmapCache.cpp)
      cli/gui_symbols.cpp   (src/slic3r/Utils/ColorSpaceConvert.cpp, deps_src/nanosvg)
      cli/CMakeLists.txt    (src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp, read at configure time; the root CMakeLists.txt)
  - scripts/ is the pipeline that fetches, builds, tests, stages and packages the engine, added
    2026-10-30 and changed 2026-10-31 (the source bundle takes the files git tracks) and
    2026-11-01 (the static runtime, which stage checks, and a cap on the dependency build's jobs).
    scripts/lib/smoke.ts carries a TypeScript port of layer-height code from
    src/libslic3r/Slicing.cpp, to predict the layers the engine must make; those portions are
    copyright the OrcaSlicer contributors.
  - protocol/ specifies the engine's command line and files, added 2026-10-31. It carries no
    OrcaSlicer code or text and is licensed under the MIT licence (protocol/LICENSE), so that any
    program may implement it.
